@node Mailboxes
@subsection Mailboxes

@cindex Mailboxes (synchronization)

Mailboxes implement a fixed size FIFO queue for passing messages
between threads without explicit locks managed by the user. A mailbox
queue length doesn't change during its lifetime. A message can be any
lisp object.

Messages are read in the same order in which they were sent. When the
queue is full, the sender blocks until a reader consumes a message,
and when the queue is empty, then the reader blocks until a sender
provides one. See @coderef{mp:mailbox-send},
@coderef{mp:mailbox-read}.

These operations have non-blocking counterparts that return @code{nil}
immediately instead of blocking in the situations described above.
See @coderef{mp:mailbox-try-send}, @coderef{mp:mailbox-try-read}.

@strong{Note:} The mailbox functions are not interrupt safe.


@node Mailboxes dictionary
@subsection Mailboxes dictionary

@cppdef ecl_make_mailbox
@deftypefun cl_object ecl_make_mailbox (cl_object name, cl_fixnum count)
@end deftypefun


@cppdef mp_make_mailbox
@lspdef mp:make-mailbox

@deftypefun cl_object mp_make_mailbox (cl_narg narg, ...)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:make-mailbox &key name count
Creates a mailbox with @var{name} and the queue's capacity of
@var{count} messages. @var{count} defaults to 128.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_name
@lspdef mp:mailbox-name

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_name (cl_object mailbox)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-name mailbox
Returns @var{mailbox} name.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_count
@lspdef mp:mailbox-count

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_count (cl_object mailbox)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-count mailbox
Returns the maximum number of messages @var{mailbox} can queue without
blocking a sender.

This value is fixed when the mailbox is created and does not reflect
the number of messages currently queued.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_empty_p
@lspdef mp:mailbox-empty-p

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_empty_p (cl_object mailbox)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-empty-p mailbox
Returns @code{t} if @var{mailbox} has zero queued messages. Otherwise
returns @code{nil}.

Do not use this function to decide whether a
subsequent @coderef{mp:mailbox-read} will block. Use
@coderef{mp:mailbox-try-read} instead.
@end defun


@cppdef ecl_mailbox_read
@lspdef mp:mailbox-read

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_read (cl_narg narg, cl_object mailbox, ...)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-read mailbox &key timeout
Returns two values. The first is a message from @var{mailbox}, or
@code{nil} if @var{timeout} expired. The second is @code{t} if a
message was actually read and @code{nil} if @var{timeout} expired.
Check the second value to distinguish a valid @code{nil} message from
an expired timeout.

Advances the queue. The message returned is the oldest one still
queued.

If @var{mailbox} is empty, blocks until a message arrives or
@var{timeout} expires. @var{timeout} is the maximum number of seconds
to wait; when it is @code{nil} (the default) the caller blocks
indefinitely.

See @coderef{mp:mailbox-try-read} for a variant which never blocks.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_try_read
@lspdef mp:mailbox-try-read

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_try_read (cl_object mailbox)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-try-read mailbox
Returns two values immediately. The first return value is a message
from @var{mailbox} or @code{nil}, if the mailbox is empty. The second
value is @code{t} if the message was actually read, and @code{nil} if
the mailbox is empty. Check the second value to distinguish a valid
@code{nil} message from an empty mailbox situation.

Advances the message queue.

This is the non-blocking variant of @coderef{mp:mailbox-read}.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_send
@lspdef mp:mailbox-send

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_send (cl_object mailbox, cl_object msg)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-send mailbox message
Sends @var{message} to @var{mailbox}. Returns @code{t} if the message
was queued and @code{nil} if @var{timeout} expired.

The message is appended at the end of the queue.

If @var{mailbox} has a number of queued messages equal to its
@coderef{mp:mailbox-count}, blocks until another thread reads a
message or @var{timeout} expires.

See @coderef{mp:mailbox-try-send} for a variant which never blocks.
@end defun


@cppdef mp_mailbox_try_send
@lspdef mp:mailbox-try-send

@deftypefun cl_object mp_mailbox_try_send (cl_object mailbox, cl_object msg)
@end deftypefun

@defun mp:mailbox-try-send mailbox message
Sends @var{message} to @var{mailbox}. Returns @code{nil} immediately if
@var{mailbox} has a number of queued messages equal to its
@coderef{mp:mailbox-count}, otherwise returns @code{t}.

This is the non-blocking variant of @coderef{mp:mailbox-send}.
@end defun

